Purpose: expose swell/core/core-ffi to privileged JS through UniFFI. Hand-written part of
the registration: exclude swell/core from the root workspace (it has its own, like gfx/wr),
depend on core-ffi from gkrust-uniffi-components, re-export its scaffolding, and list its
async/sync configuration under its crate name in config.toml. Cargo.lock gains only the
four swell core crates; every third-party dependency is already vendored.
Test: ./mach build, then ./mach test swell/tests/xpcshell (and cargo test in swell/core).
Companion: 0021 holds the regenerated output.
Upstreamable: no.

